## results
## step 1: g1 was created while the policy allowed only k014-m1 (the only place it could be scheduled; its location was not printed before the change).
##         After widening the policy to three clusters
##         (a placement change) the unit was on k014-m2. kind-G7 records the same operation with before and after: a Running unit was moved.
## step 2: on k014-m2 there was room for one more whole set, so the resized unit stayed (kthena recreated its Pods: new revision).
## step 3: k014-m2 had 1 free GPU, not enough for another whole set of the resized unit (2 GPU); the scheduler MOVED the unit to k014-m3
##         although it was shrinking in place. The estimate for a unit's own cluster does not add back what the unit already uses.
## side observation in step 3: h4 and h5 were left unscheduled although k014-m3 had room for one more unit at that time.
